Ultraviolet Disinfection Guidance Manual — US EPA (@wu-uv-epa: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_1X6EKSQ3HSS90RN9N9289MQNNX
US EPA, Office of Water. EPA 815-R-06-007, November 2006, 436 PDF pages. [Official PDF](https://www.epa.gov/system/files/documents/2022-10/ultraviolet-disinfection-guidance-manual-2006.pdf).

Read chapters 2–6 from UV fundamentals through planning, design, reactor validation and operation. Study chapter 5 and the worked validation examples closely, then critique an identified reactor report against its stated operating envelope. Pair this manual with the 2022 toolkit instead of assuming the original guidance covers every later method.

The cover, contents and selected validation material were inspected on 30 October 2026. This is technical guidance, not a regulation or proof that a device works. The publicly hosted document credits contracted authors and other contributors; retain its attribution and separately credited material notices. Laboratory and field validation require competent facilities; the trail's exercises can use published measurements and reports.
